 {"id":"fabro-019d","title":"Deploy + smoke: pick up fabro-900e context envelope (dc5959a80) via just up","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T10:01:51.011Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-27T12:05:55.500Z","description":"Blocked 2026-08-27: Docker Desktop backend on the Windows host was down (no /var/run/docker.sock, no docker.sock in the docker-desktop guest-services mount, no passwordless sudo), so the just up pipeline failed at build-image after the SPA refresh. Code is committed on denkhaus (dc5959a80), full test suites green. When Docker Desktop is running: just up (smoke 7/7 expected), then verify a run.notice context_update_dropped appears on the first envelope-owning workflow. Lab adoption is separate: set context_allow_keys/context_append_keys on the develop planner node at the next lab sync (meta/denkhaus-lab).","labels":["workflows"],"closedAt":"2026-08-27T12:05:55.500Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-cd27","title":"server: PR content generation has no retry — glm-5.3 non-JSON response forces deterministic fallback","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T15:15:53.997Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T22:12:13.319Z","description":"FIX LANDED 2026-09-03 (commit 989038c48, deployed same day): catalog declares glm-4.7 reasoning=true + effort levels low/high/max (was mislabeled non-reasoning — the root of the un-pinned full-reasoning PR calls); pr_content_effort defaults unconfigured reasoning-capable models to Low (configured wins, unknown models send nothing); generate_object unwraps one whole-payload markdown fence and reports the response head (first 200 chars) in NoObjectGenerated; generate_pr_content runs one structured attempt + one plain retry (no response_format) with lenient JSON parse, then prose salvage as PR body with deterministic title, then skeleton fallback. Twin tests: retry-success, retry-then-salvage, fallback (pipeline::pull_request), fence + head units (fabro-llm generate), effort units (glm-4.7/glm-5.3 -> Low). clippy -D warnings clean, 2395 tests green.\n\nDONE-WHEN REMAINS: one live develop run publishing an LLM-written PR body via glm-4.7 (verification run queued after deploy; candidate fib seed: gofib test builder refactor from run 01M1MHGS7PH26EP20B2RTAPN4G journal observation).\n\nHistorical context: root cause of the glm-5.3-era failures was publish.rs passing pr_model instead of pr_resolved_model (fixed 2026-08-27, sentinel test). ZAI API PROBE 2026-09-03 (88KB-diff matrix): response_format json_schema IS sent and honored (6/6 probes clean JSON); glm-4.7 rejects enable_thinking=false with code 1210; thinking:{type:disabled} accepted-but-weakened on glm-4.7, fully honored on glm-5.3; reasoning_effort=low -> zero reasoning, 5x faster. Failure mode was probabilistic under full reasoning (fenced/prefixed JSON).","labels":["workflows"],"closedAt":"2026-09-03T22:12:13.319Z","closeReason":"DONE 2026-09-03. Fix landed in 989038c48 (catalog: glm-4.7 reasoning=true + effort levels low/high/max; pr_content_effort low-default for reasoning-capable models; generate_object fence-unwrap + response head in NoObjectGenerated; generate_pr_content structured attempt + plain retry + prose salvage). Twin tests: retry-success, retry-then-salvage, fallback. LIVE PROOF: run 01M1MMK5C6B313SY70Y2EPKE82 published PR #13 with an LLM-written body via glm-4.7 (\"Every flag combination in fib_test.go needed its own wrapper...\") — no FALLBACK_BODY_NOTICE, auto-merged into denkhaus-lab (a08304909). Related open seeds: fabro-2e66 (degradation surfacing / auto-merge preflight), fabro-e7e5 (control degrade + future thinking-off mapping)."}
 {"id":"fabro-1cac","title":"engine: materialize run warnings/errors into the worktree (.fabro/logs/) at run finalization","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T15:15:54.089Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-27T17:54:39.411Z","description":"User ask (2026-08-27, after run 01M11P68SHFS): errors and warnings that appear in the worker tracing log should be persisted under .fabro/ in the repository BY THE WORKFLOW, not via an external just command after the fact.\n\nToday:\n- Per-run tracing logs ARE persisted server-side (Storage::runtime_directory().logs_dir(); fabro logs <run-id> reads them — WARN lines like write_locks and PR-content fallback are all there).\n- But they never reach the repo: the run branch/PR carries no record, and the improve review (which consumes events, not tracing) cannot see them. Events-vs-tracing separation stays per events-strategy.md — this is NOT a request for warning Event variants.\n\nDesign (journal precedent fabro-31b2 — the stage-journal bridge hands context_updates to hooks):\n- At run finalization, the worker extracts WARN/ERROR lines from its own per-run tracing log (the file it already writes to logs_dir) and writes a digest .fabro/logs/<run-id>/warnings.md into the SANDBOX WORKTREE (header: run id, stage attribution where the span carries one, raw line otherwise).\n- The final worktree commit then carries the digest onto the run branch -> PR -> base branch; the improve review and humans see it in-repo.\n- Size-bounded (cap the digest; full log stays in server storage) and failure-never-breaks-the-run (side-effect only, like the journal hook).\n\nWhy not a run_complete hook: sandbox hooks cannot reach the server log store (d810: no fabro CLI/server access inside the product sandbox); host hooks write on the server host, not into the sandbox worktree — only the engine sits on both sides.\n\nOpen design question (user decision): should product-facing degradations (PR-content fallback used, Slack notification failed) ALSO become run events so fabro events/improve see them without file indirection? Events-strategy says events are product-facing state transitions — the PR-fallback arguably qualifies; discuss before implementing.\n\nDone when a twin develop run's run branch contains .fabro/logs/<run-id>/warnings.md with the injected WARN lines, and a red-injected run shows its errors there too.","labels":["workflows"],"closedAt":"2026-08-27T17:54:39.411Z","closeReason":"Superseded by the Workflow-Revisor design (ADR-0011, grill 2026-08-27): live read-only tools replace materialized archives. Per-run tracing logs already persist server-side (fabro logs); the revisor reaches them via the new fabro_run_logs tool for Ask-Fabro analysts (follow-up seed). No engine materialization of logs/metrics into the worktree; no warning events (events-vs-tracing separation stays)."}
